	       VCRAPS -- display-oriented casino craps	    CRAPSLIB -- interface-independent craps engineThis package contains crapslib and vcraps.  Crapslib is aninterface-independent craps-game library; vcraps is a curses-basedinterface built on top of crapslib.The game is a full implementation of professional casino-style craps.Vcraps provides on-line help in the form of the '?' key.  For rules ofplay and betting, plus interesting strategies to minimize the "houseadvantage," please refer to Edwin Silberstang's excellent book,"Winning Casino Craps".The "table" is a one-dollar table (i.e., all bets are in multiples of$1).  By default, vcraps starts you off with a bankroll of $1,000 in acasino offering double free odds.  The -b<bankroll> command-lineswitch can be used to start with a different bankroll.  The -s switchmeans use single free odds.Vcraps input can be interrupted at any time with the escape key orcontrol-L; the latter redraws the screen.  Messages appear at thebottom of the screen and must be cleared by pressing the spacebar.Some casinos pay different bets differently.  Vcraps offers a singleconfiguration of payoffs, but other clients of crapslib can configurethe payoffs that vary.  (The varying payoffs are Big 6, Big 8, Field,and the one-roll bets on 2, 3, 11, and 12.)The bets and payoffs are as follows:Pass-line                           1-1.Free odds on pass-line              2-1 for 4 and 10,                                    3-2 for 5 and 9,                                    6-5 for 6 and 8.Come                                1-1.Free odds on a come number          2-1 for 4 and 10,                                    3-2 for 5 and 9,                                    6-5 for 6 and 8.Don't pass (bar 12)                 1-1.Free odds on don't pass             1-2 for 4 and 10,                                    2-3 for 5 and 9,                                    5-6 for 6 and 8.Don't come (bar 12)                 1-1.Free odds on a don't come number    1-2 for 4 and 10,                                    2-3 for 5 and 9,                                    5-6 for 6 and 8.Place numbers                       9-5 for 4 and 10 (2-1 if bought),                                    7-5 for 5 and 9,                                    7-6 for 6 and 8.    (Buying the 4 or 10 requires a 5% commission on the wager.)Don't place numbers                 1-2 for 4 and 10,                                    2-3 for 5 and 9,                                    5-6 for 6 and 8.    (Don't-place wagers require a 5% commission on the possible payoff.)Big 6 and Big 8                     1-1    (Some casinos pay 6-5.)Field                               1-1 for 3, 4, 9, 10, and 11,                                    2-1 for 2 and 12.    (Some casinos pay 3-1 on either the 2 or the 12.)Hardway bets                        7-1 for 4 and 10,                                    9-1 for 6 and 8.One-roll bets                       29-1 for 2 and 12,                                    14-1 for 3 and 11.    (Some casinos pay 30-1 and 15-1.)Any 7                               4-1.Any Craps                           7-1.Author:  Bob Glickstein (bobg@andrew.cmu.edu)  August 1990This program is in the public domain.